    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing our undisputed anchor; his 65.56 score is buoyed by an elite .423 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Matthews, making him the primary candidate for offensive production. We also see significant value in **Casey Schmitt** (59.53) and **Christian Yelich** (59.01). The decision to play **Christian Yelich** is particularly nuanced; while his raw projections are modest, the \"slow delivery\" factor of the opposing pitcher creates a high-probability environment for him to steal a bag, which is vital given our scarcity-focused strategy. Similarly, **Casey Schmitt** benefits from a high-leverage lineup slot (#3) that should maximize his counting stat potential against Ryne Nelson.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved balancing the upside of **Junior Caminero** (50.78) against the reliability of our lower-scoring starters. While **Junior Caminero** possesses premium talent, the matchup against Bradish (xERA 3.05) suppressed his efficiency enough that he sits at the bottom of our active rotation, narrowly edging out **Dillon Dingler** (49.44). We are monitoring the status of **Casey Schmitt**, **Chase Meidroth**, and **Hyeseong Kim** closely; their scores are currently based on projected lineup slots. Should the official orders shift these players down the lineup, we will need to account for a recalibration of their scores. Furthermore, while **Caleb Durbin** carries an elevated score (54.70) due to a weak opposing starter in Falter, he is handicapped by an unfavorable #9 batting position and incoming wind at the venue, which warrants tempered expectations for his total output.",
